  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="cb68031b-9aaf-5364-96ea-a2dde058661e" activityNameId="b7bdc56d-f85e-53cc-b064-8ee62911a90e" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Silicon, solar grade, fluidised bed reactor (FBR), at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Silicon, solar grade, fluidised bed reactor (FBR), at plant
Process for FBR is based on the Siemens process with an adjusted electricity demand (30% of Siemens Process) according to de Wild-Scholten &amp; Alsema 2005;
CAS number: 7440-21-3; 
Formula: Si; 
Synonyms: SoG-Silicon, polycrystaline; 
UUID: 10fa705a-2e57-3ed5-925e-4ae2cdd74f62
Gate to gate inventory for the production of high purity polycrystalline silicon from MG-silicon in FBR. Emissions and ressource uses are only roughly estimated.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: No actual data for FBR technology available, estimation based on the Siemens process with reduced electricity demand
Time period: Time of investigation
Production volume: 14400 t worldwide in 2005
Sampling: Average of data from one company and estimated data from another company based on literature data 
Extrapolations: Emissions to water are estimated with figures investigated for MG-silicon purification to EG-silicon with a similar type of process. Extrapolation of European LCI inventory data by changing the consumed electricity mix to the Chinese electricity mix.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_10fa705a-2e57-3ed5-925e-4ae2cdd74f62.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
